ee-quarter position, 35 degrees to her right and about 10 degrees above her eyes. Her head retains this readable angle as her eyes briefly meet the lens. Frame the whole head through below the waist in a vertical photograph, keeping the top of the head, the right temple, the gathering root and the complete hanging tail clear. A moderate portrait lens and sufficient depth of field keep face and hair connections resolved together, with the workbench readable and the farther plants softly receding. Natural skin texture, individual hair strands, damp paper edges and worn wood give the scene the specificity of an inhabited photographic moment.",
